openbrain-client.local.yaml
# local MCP server config (per-machine; not part of the module)
.mcp.json
.codex/
.logs
.devtools/
bin/
# run-queue per-unit worktrees are rooted under <repo>/worktrees/; never track them
worktrees/
.claude/legacy/
# Catalog-materialized skills are NOT tracked: gold owns them, so gold stays the only
# source and a skill withdrawn there stops reaching this repo by definition. A worktree
# still gets them -- keel/requirement-157 replication copies the gitignored matches from
# the primary checkout on bring-up. See .claude/README.md.
#
# The five negations below are the locally-authored skills. They are repo files under
# the change-control rule in CLAUDE.md, and a tracked file is never replicated, so they
# cannot be shadowed by a copy. The list is maintained BY HAND: the real discriminator
# is the x-openbrain-content-hash stamp in a skill's front matter, and a gitignore rule
# cannot read file contents.
#
# Maintenance: a new catalog skill needs no change here -- it is ignored on arrival. A
# new locally-authored skill needs its own negation line, or it stays invisible to git.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/asd-ste100/
!.claude/skills/build/
!.claude/skills/decide/
!.claude/skills/merge/
!.claude/skills/publish/
# .claude/agents/ stays tracked pending the follow-on named in keel/issue-235.
.claude/materialization.json
# gitignored sandbox for `openbrain-client init --dev` (KD10, CR-0249)
consumer-claude/

# DHF-REQ: keel/requirement-80
# When built in the wrong location
/keel-dev
/keel-demo
.vscode/test-lanes.json
desired-state.json
discover.json
# per-machine /usage-report snapshots (personal spend/session data; never in public history)
docs/usage/

scratchpad/

# CodeGraph index (per-machine code intelligence store; not part of the module)
.codegraph/
# openbrain-client init transcript
init.log
# ad-hoc tool report output
report.json
